description:
FILED s521 (Fable, 2026-10-18 18:0x) from the s521a merge probes (review/p521a/b5-cvflags.pl + scratchpad rv/cvf.pl): on the s521a tip and on the ed8a4504 base alike,
    use B qw(svref_2object CVf_ANON);
    print B::CVf_ANON(), " ", CVf_ANON(), " ", CVf_ANON, "\n";
perl 5.40.3: `128 128 128`.  PCL: `128 128 CVf_ANON` -- the bare imported constant is a bareword STRING, so `$flags & CVf_ANON` is `$flags & 0` = 0 and every masked read through the bare spelling is silently wrong (the qualified call and the parenthesised call are right).  PRE-EXISTING (identical on the base); the #3362 fix is not affected (perl's own t/op/stash.t spells `B::CVf_ANON()`).

CAUSE: lib/B.pm line ~73 `our @EXPORT_OK = (sort(keys %CONST), ...)` -- the export list is COMPUTED from a hash, so Pl's static export scan (which reads literal qw() lists, docs/static-parse-limits-review-s512.md) cannot see the CVf_* / SVf_* names, and an imported ()-prototype constant that the parse does not know is not a TERM (#365's rule applies only to names the scan can see).  FIX (shim side, rule 9a): spell @EXPORT_OK literally in lib/B.pm (the %CONST keys written out as a qw() list, kept in sync by a one-line test that compares the two) -- then the bare spelling is a call.  Probe the three spellings = perl; a guard row in Pl/t/b-shim-01.t (the bare spelling), inverse-verified.  LOW; a filler.  (The generic half -- a computed @EXPORT_OK in ANY module -- is #3143 / the #2610 run-time detector, not this task.)
